.TH MONOTEST 1
.SH NAME
monotest \- self-test for the Monocypher module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B monotest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Monotest
exercises
.IR mono (2)
and prints one line per test: BLAKE2b against the specification's
digest of
.RB ` "abc" ','
an XChaCha20-Poly1305 round trip with a tampered tag and a tampered
associated-data value, X25519 agreement between two key pairs, and
EdDSA sign, verify and rejection of a changed message.
It raises
.B fail:tests
if any test fails, so it can gate a build:
.IP
.EX
; monotest || echo crypto is broken
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/monotest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR mono (2)
